# Environment reference for angular-ecommerce-3d
#
# Local development & Docker both use backend/.env as the source of truth:
#   cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# Required before first run (see docs/GETTING_STARTED.md):
#   DATABASE_*  — PostgreSQL connection
#   JWT_SECRET  — min 32 chars (openssl rand -base64 48). Docker Compose sets
#                 NODE_ENV=production, so a short/placeholder secret will exit(1).
#   ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD — for POST /api/auth/create-admin
#
# Docker Compose:
#   - Loads backend/.env via env_file
#   - Overrides DATABASE_HOST=postgres, DATABASE_SSL=false, TYPEORM_SYNCHRONIZE=true
#   - Builds backend from repo root (npm workspaces) — see backend/Dockerfile
#   - Frontend on http://localhost:4200 (nginx proxies /api and /uploads)
#   - Port conflicts: POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5434 BACKEND_HOST_PORT=3003 FRONTEND_HOST_PORT=4201
#
# Optional root .env overrides for the postgres service only:
#
# DATABASE_USERNAME=postgres
# DATABASE_PASSWORD=postgres
# DATABASE_NAME=ecommerce_db
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5432
# Frontend payment keys are configured at runtime in Admin → Settings.
# Leave src/environments/environment.prod.ts payment fields empty for production builds.
